<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/coccolith-emiliania-calcite-rosette-1> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Young et al. (1992) V/R Alternating Crystal Ring Parity & Orthogonal c-Axes Law" ;
    dct:description "Establishes that the proto-coccolith ring nucleates exactly 2*N_seg alternating V-unit (vertical c-axis) and R-unit (radial c-axis) calcite crystals whose c-axes are strictly orthogonal (90 deg) around the entire baseplate periphery | Variables: N_seg: radial coccolith shield segment count; N_total = 2*N_seg: alternating V and R calcite crystal nuclei on the proto-coccolith ring; c_V, c_R: calcite [0001] crystallographic c-axis vectors" ;
    dct:source "Young et al. (1992) Nature 356:516-518; Didymus et al. (1993) Proc. R. Soc. B 252:259-264" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/HEAD/2022-coccolith-emiliania-calcite-rosette.py#L130-L245>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/HEAD/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_080_emiliania_calcite_rosette.lean#L27-L87> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def vr_total_nuclei (n_seg : Nat) : Nat := 2 * n_seg
def v_unit_c_axis (cz : Int) : Vec3Int := { x := 0, y := 0, z := cz }
def r_unit_c_axis (rx ry : Int) : Vec3Int := { x := rx, y := ry, z := 0 }
theorem vr_crystal_ring_parity_and_orthogonal_c_axes :
    vr_total_nuclei 32 = 64 ∧ (vr_total_nuclei 32) % 2 = 0 ∧
    vec3_dot (v_unit_c_axis 1) (r_unit_c_axis 3 4) = 0 := by decide
"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "N_total = 2 * N_seg (N_V = N_R = N_seg, N_total mod 2 = 0)  and  c_V . c_R(theta_k) = (0,0,1) . (cos theta_k, sin theta_k, 0) = 0" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1038/356516a0>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/ncomms11904>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-018-04168-9>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rspb.1993.0073> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Young et al. (1992) V/R Bimodal Calcite Crystallographic Nucleation Ring (N_total = 2*N_seg, c_V . c_R = 0), Linear Proto-Coccolith Circumference Scaling & Jaya et al. (2016) Spherical Coccosphere Euler Interlocking Packing" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_080.vr_total_nuclei" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_080.vr_crystal_ring_parity_and_orthogonal_c_axes" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/coccolith-emiliania-calcite-rosette-2> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Linear Proto-Coccolith Ring Circumference & Distal Shield Length Scaling Law" ;
    dct:description "Proves that conserved crystal nucleation spacing w_0 on the organic baseplate rim forces proto-coccolith ring circumference and distal shield diameter L_d to scale linearly with segment count N_seg across morphotypes C, R, A, B/C, and B | Variables: N_seg: radial segment number; w_0 = 0.145 um: conserved R/V crystal pair nucleation pitch; R_tube: central tube radius; L_d: distal shield major axis length" ;
    dct:source "Young et al. (1992) Nature 356:516-518; Didymus et al. (1993) Proc. R. Soc. B 252:259-264" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/HEAD/2022-coccolith-emiliania-calcite-rosette.py#L248-L355>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/HEAD/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_080_emiliania_calcite_rosette.lean#L93-L133> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def proto_ring_circumference_nm (n_seg w_nm : Nat) : Nat := n_seg * w_nm
def distal_shield_scaled_nm (n_seg w_nm two_pi_l_spoke_nm : Nat) : Nat :=
  proto_ring_circumference_nm n_seg w_nm + two_pi_l_spoke_nm
theorem proto_coccolith_circumference_and_distal_shield_linear_scaling :
    proto_ring_circumference_nm 33 145 - proto_ring_circumference_nm 32 145 = 145 ∧
    distal_shield_scaled_nm 26 145 6355 < distal_shield_scaled_nm 32 145 6355 ∧
    distal_shield_scaled_nm 32 145 6355 < distal_shield_scaled_nm 38 145 6355 := by decide
"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "C_ring(N_seg) = N_seg * w_0  =>  R_tube = (N_seg * w_0)/(2*pi)  and  L_d(N_seg) = (N_seg * w_0)/pi + 2*L_spoke" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1038/356516a0>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/ncomms11904>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-018-04168-9>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rspb.1993.0073> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Young et al. (1992) V/R Bimodal Calcite Crystallographic Nucleation Ring (N_total = 2*N_seg, c_V . c_R = 0), Linear Proto-Coccolith Circumference Scaling & Jaya et al. (2016) Spherical Coccosphere Euler Interlocking Packing" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_080.distal_shield_scaled_nm" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_080.proto_coccolith_circumference_and_distal_shield_linear_scaling" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/coccolith-emiliania-calcite-rosette-3> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Spherical Euler Polyhedral Packing & Trivalent Interlocking Coccosphere Law" ;
    dct:description "Governs the 3D topological closure and load-sharing overlap edge count E = 3*(N_cocc - 2) of interlocking spherical coccospheres under compressive loading | Variables: F = N_cocc: number of interlocking coccolith shields tiling the coccosphere; V: triple-coccolith junction vertices; E: pairwise overlapping suture edges; chi = 2: spherical Euler characteristic" ;
    dct:source "Jaya et al. (2016) Nat. Commun. 7:11904; Walker et al. (2018) Nat. Commun. 9:1-12" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/HEAD/2022-coccolith-emiliania-calcite-rosette.py#L358-L455>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/HEAD/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_080_emiliania_calcite_rosette.lean#L139-L185> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def coccosphere_vertices (f_cocc : Int) : Int := 2 * (f_cocc - 2)
def coccosphere_edges (f_cocc : Int) : Int := 3 * (f_cocc - 2)
def coccosphere_euler_characteristic (f_cocc : Int) : Int :=
  coccosphere_vertices f_cocc - coccosphere_edges f_cocc + f_cocc
theorem coccosphere_euler_polyhedral_packing_and_trivalent_interlock :
    coccosphere_euler_characteristic 16 = 2 ∧
    3 * coccosphere_vertices 16 = 2 * coccosphere_edges 16 ∧
    coccosphere_edges 16 = 42 := by decide
"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "V - E + F = 2 on S^2 with 3*V = 2*E  =>  V = 2*(N_cocc - 2), E = 3*(N_cocc - 2) for F = N_cocc in [12, 24]" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1038/356516a0>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/ncomms11904>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-018-04168-9>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rspb.1993.0073> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Young et al. (1992) V/R Bimodal Calcite Crystallographic Nucleation Ring (N_total = 2*N_seg, c_V . c_R = 0), Linear Proto-Coccolith Circumference Scaling & Jaya et al. (2016) Spherical Coccosphere Euler Interlocking Packing" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_080.coccosphere_euler_characteristic" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_080.coccosphere_euler_polyhedral_packing_and_trivalent_interlock" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/coccolith-emiliania-calcite-rosette-4> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "CAP-Polysaccharide T-Shaped Hammer-Head Expansion vs Ocean Acidification Truncation Law" ;
    dct:description "Explains why ocean acidification (Omega_calcite < 1) or loss of acidic CAP polysaccharides truncates distal T-shaped hammer heads and destroys inter-spoke rim interlocking | Variables: w_spoke: radial spoke shaft width; w_head: outer T-shaped hammer-head tangential width; Omega_calcite: seawater/vesicle calcite saturation state; c_CAP: coccolith-associated polysaccharide activity" ;
    dct:source "Didymus et al. (1993) Proc. R. Soc. B 252:259-264; Jaya et al. (2016) Nat. Commun. 7:11904; Walker et al. (2018) Nat. Commun. 9:1-12" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/HEAD/2022-coccolith-emiliania-calcite-rosette.py#L458-L535>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/HEAD/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_080_emiliania_calcite_rosette.lean#L191-L231> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def calcite_supersat_excess (omega_scaled : Nat) : Nat :=
  if omega_scaled > 100 then omega_scaled - 100 else 0
def hammer_head_width_scaled (w_spoke cap_pct omega_scaled : Nat) : Nat :=
  w_spoke * 100 + (w_spoke * cap_pct * calcite_supersat_excess omega_scaled) / 100
theorem cap_polysaccharide_hammer_expansion_and_acidification_truncation :
    hammer_head_width_scaled 100 28 75 = 10000 ∧
    hammer_head_width_scaled 100 0 420 = 10000 ∧
    hammer_head_width_scaled 100 28 420 > hammer_head_width_scaled 100 28 75 := by decide
"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "w_head(Omega_calcite, c_CAP) = w_spoke * (1 + alpha_T * c_CAP * max(Omega_calcite - 1, 0))  =>  w_head = w_spoke when Omega_calcite <= 1 or c_CAP = 0" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1038/356516a0>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/ncomms11904>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-018-04168-9>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rspb.1993.0073> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Young et al. (1992) V/R Bimodal Calcite Crystallographic Nucleation Ring (N_total = 2*N_seg, c_V . c_R = 0), Linear Proto-Coccolith Circumference Scaling & Jaya et al. (2016) Spherical Coccosphere Euler Interlocking Packing" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_080.hammer_head_width_scaled" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_080.cap_polysaccharide_hammer_expansion_and_acidification_truncation" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

